{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Arbeh.</b> From the language of multiplicity." "<b>Salam.</b> A species that climbs on rocks." "<b>Chargol.</b> If it is one word it has no brother, and if it is two words like the word לפלמוני, its derivation is the reverse of the derivation of Salam." "<b>Chagav.</b> Known from the Ishmaelite language."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {2 "Reading מרובעת as 'one word' (a single quadrilateral form); if the reading were מרובע in the sense of 'square,' the argument would be obscure. Alternatively, 'מרובעת' may mean 'a quadriliteral,' i.e., a word with no Hebrew cognate."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:30.618338753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}